==Battleground==
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**30 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**5 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 1.33~2.67 seconds<sup>40f~80f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Flying Ninja Cat (Enemy)|Flying Ninja Cat]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Stall the first Brollow for cash, then use generic meatshield spam to kill the Brollow horde. Once the spam dies down, you can use [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] to deal with Flying Ninja Cat. If you have [[Cameraman Cat]], she absolutely beats up the entire stage with her 10 range advantage against Flying Ninja Cat and her Area Attack allowing her to deal quite well with the Brollow spam. You may also include [[Octopus Cat|Octopus Cat]] to tank the Brollows and Flying Ninja in addition to weakening them. If you want the absolute safety net, [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] stands from a safe range and can completely freeze Flying Ninja to where it won't do a thing, though this is best saved for the cleanup or if you can manage to juggle the Brollows effectively without them dealing too much damage from rebounds.

